l/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"content_type":"application/json","state":"uploaded","size":653,"digest":"sha256:376a6a5dd5def185377ff1611077969729ede4806347a97b4966b6508ee66f54","download_count":0,"created_at":"2026-11-18T05:17:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-18T05:17:56Z","browser_download_url":"https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/releases/download/m136-v0.13.6/m13stage6-starter-manifest.json"}],"tarball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/tarball/m136-v0.13.6","zipball_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/enginsoysal/engacer-os/zipball/m136-v0.13.6","body":"# Engacer OS M13.6 / 0.13.6 - Familiar Start, taskbar and system tray\n\nThis release qualifies the named Start/taskbar/tray and native display profiles within M13-STAGE6-VM-v1. Later M13 stages and the final M13.12 integration remain separate. Read the [installation guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/270e8cbb233519db14de4278febc4bf57237cbd7/docs/handbook/install-m136.md), [Start/taskbar/tray guide](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/270e8cbb233519db14de4278febc4bf57237cbd7/docs/handbook/start-m136.md) and [stage decisions](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/270e8cbb233519db14de4278febc4bf57237cbd7/docs/milestones/m13-6.md).\n\n## Download and verify\n\nUse the exact ISO or extract the complete prepared VMware ZIP and open EngacerOS.vmx. Keep all supplied devices enabled, UEFI and Secure Boot off. The growable blank 20-GiB SATA disk is not preinstalled. Select I Copied It if VMware asks.\n\n- Build: `43fb63246919e57cbca51fb54bdc4be1`.\n- ISO SHA256: `9817308547a48622c02ef17f83d4b7b58078c29c317670ad9a380752f55d71b5`.\n- VMware ZIP SHA256: `37078030ab0844f1d7556b17d9728e90cd220e29a0e87056ca02db1825e656fc`.\n\nThe twenty assets include both exact-media manifests, boot/installed images and maps, checksums, notices and applicable third-party source/license material. The build binds 603 compiled source inputs. Immutable font masks remain 251,248 bytes; fixed desktop state remains 553,436 bytes and fixed installer state remains 48,412 bytes. Completed named tasks retain zero managed pages and idle CPUs halt. Configured RAM, framebuffer storage and managed current/peak/retained pages are distinct.\n\n## What changes\n\nPinned apps and folders use original 40-unit icons with centered measured labels. Search stays local, immediate and bounded; All apps, explicit Grid/List and optional categories retain ordinary keyboard navigation, pinning and per-user customization. Shared tile geometry drives the drawn items, hit targets, arrow neighbors and pagination. No indexing worker or process per keystroke is added.\n\nTaskbar app groups use a quieter 112-unit stride, recognizable icons, short labels and real window-count badges. Unopened/running/active/all-minimized states follow actual windows. Stable pin/MRU order, generation-bound window choices, dirty-work reviews and bounded overflow preserve access. A white keyboard-focus outline remains visible against the dark taskbar. Supported left/center alignment moves both launch surfaces and persists independently.\n\nSystem flyouts retain real wired-network/USB/audio/UTC-calendar providers. Replacing a USB device cannot inherit an old held action; safe removal waits for its flush. Software PCM changes during an owned picker stay session-only. Unsupported Wi-Fi, Bluetooth and battery providers remain explicitly unavailable.\n\n## Exact native qualification\n\nThe matching acceptance and resource records describe the actual named task/profile checks. Five physical display/control/Start profiles include ordinary 1920x1080, compact 1280x800, 1024x768, 1920x1200 at 150% and actual 3840x2160 at 200%. Real local search/launch, categories, pins, Grid/List, optional-app removal/reinstall, actual folder pinning, light/dark/high contrast, power cancellation and independent disk starts bind these media.\n\nThe taskbar phase exercises two Files windows, an owner-bound dirty Editor/picker, pin/unpin/reorder, optional-app refusal/removal, eight live apps, overflow and correct quota refusal. Its original final-start assertion retained the older six-visible-group expectation; the matching new layout correctly shows all eight pins. The failed observation remains diagnostic, with an explicit successful continuation consisting of two fresh no-ISO starts, exact saved preference bytes and real minimize/restore. No historical failure is rewritten.\n\nActual USB provider replacement, safe removal, independently checked imported bytes, volume persistence, no-device/unavailable states and USB/PS2 shortcuts are tested separately. Left/center/left/center layout changes and two independent high-resolution starts inspect exact persisted preference bytes and actual targets.\n\nThe exact enabled-device SATA/UEFI VMware package performs real installation, retained-ISO startup and two disk-only starts with unchanged user VM inventory. This is not a new fourteen-controller qualification. [Acceptance](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/270e8cbb233519db14de4278febc4bf57237cbd7/evidence/M13/6/acceptance-results.json), [resources](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/270e8cbb233519db14de4278febc4bf57237cbd7/evidence/M13/6/resources.json), [visual review](https://github.com/enginsoysal/engacer-os/blob/270e8cbb233519db14de4278febc4bf57237cbd7/evidence/M13/6/visual-review.json).\n\n## Scope and observations\n\nA persistent pin notice can cover a caption at compact sizes; use its visible Dismiss before that caption. The native hit guard correctly prevents clicking through the message. M13.8 carries the notification-positioning refinement. Original failed candidates and test observations remain explicitly excluded diagnostics.\n\nRead-only test settling distinguishes a completed mutation from the next rendered list and hover paint from completion of the later input edge. It does not force Refresh or change guest memory. Host settling intervals are not native feedback latency, display FPS or M13.9 qualification.\n\nWhole-disk installation keeps explicit erasure consent. Data-preserving resize/dual boot, Secure Boot signing, universal physical hardware, vendor GPU 3D and general MS-DOS/Windows compatibility remain outside this stage. Agent scenarios and visual review are separate from human novice research. Public GitHub/website closure is recorded separately after the exact release is published.\n"}